BEGINTEXT

                           The Nebula, ver 1.0
                              By Adam Luker

     It is easy to lose one's bearings, deep in the heart of the Forestine 
 Nebula. It is easy to be blinded by the dust, and lose one's connections
 to life Outside.

     For the regional governers assigned to this part of the First Great 
 Empire, it was all too easy to forget their allegiances and turn to 
 despotism or piracy, leaving behind their noble pasts and allowing wealth
 and power to displace justice and right. And so they abandoned their roles
 as protectors of the peace and severed their relations with the galaxial 
 core.

     And so it was that the Forestine Nebula was not part of the spasmic
 collapse of the empire. Deep in the heart of the nebula, humanity didn't 
 undergo the cataclysmic fall. But they dwindled. As blinded by greed and 
 selfishness as they were by the clouds that surrounded them, the nebulaic
 planetary systems spent their strength in wars, their wit in intrigue, their
 intelligence in the undermining of others, until the remnant receded into
 themselves and retreated from interaction with others.

NEWPAGE

     You control one of the eight empires have risen from the wreckage. 
 As you explore the nebula around you, you will find resources that will aid
 you in your expansion. Your goal is to conquer the other empires in the 
 nebula and forge the seed of a New Great Empire, which must grow past the
 confines of this nebula and fill the entire galaxy.

     But first things first: become the only viable power in the nebula.

ENDTEXT

BEGINDESCRIPTION

